{
  "__comment": "Parity fixture for trimBreadcrumbs(crumbs, options). Consumed by TS (sdk-core), Swift (sdk-ios), and Kotlin (sdk-android) tests. All three implementations must produce byte-identical output arrays for every case. See packages/sdk-core/src/breadcrumbs/trim.ts for the reference implementation and the public behavior contract §4 for the algorithm.",
  "__costModel": "cost(crumb) = 64 + message.length + dataCost(data). dataCost: string=length, number|boolean=8, null=4, array=2+sum(item+2), object=2+sum(key.length+value+2), absent data=0. ALL lengths are UTF-16 code units (JS .length, Swift utf16.count, Kotlin String.length).",
  "__semantics": "INPUT INVARIANT: no two crumbs share the same (t, seq) pair — determinism (and Swift's non-stable sort) depends on it. 1) console messages over consoleEntryCap are middle-spliced to first cap/2 + '…[+N chars]…' + last cap/2 and flagged truncated:true; error crumbs' data.stackDigest is capped to its first 10 newline-separated lines and flagged truncated:true. 2) The newest entry of every kind present is always kept. 3) While total cost > byteBudget, evict the oldest console/network crumb; only when none remain, evict the oldest structural (navigation/tap/lifecycle/error/custom). 4) Each kind that lost entries gets ONE marker {t,seq of its newest dropped entry, level:'info', message:'+N <kind> hidden', data:{droppedCount:N}}; markers do not count against the budget. 5) Output sorted by (t, seq). 6) After byte eviction, if more than 121 entries remain (121 = 128 protocol payload.breadcrumbs maxItems minus 7 worst-case one-marker-per-kind), evict further in the same order (oldest console/network first, then oldest structural, skipping the newest-of-kind must-keeps) until 121 remain; markers then apply as in step 4. 7) Both eviction passes can fire in one run (too large for a literal fixture case — see the ported 'combined byte-eviction + count-cap' unit test per SDK): the byte pass runs first and evicts bulky crumbs down to budget, then the count pass continues down the SAME eviction order (oldest bulky, then oldest structural, skipping must-keeps) until kept ≤ 121; because both passes share that order, a kind whose non-must-keep members are entirely bulky-evicted before the count target is reached will show the identical dropped count even under an unbounded byte budget — the count pass alone would evict it.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "under-budget-passthrough",
      "options": {
        "byteBudget": 16384,
        "consoleEntryCap": 1024
      },
      "input": [
        {
          "t": 1,
          "seq": 0,
          "kind": "navigation",
          "message": "nav-to-home"
        },
        {
          "t": 2,
          "seq": 1,
          "kind": "console",
          "message": "hello world"
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "t": 1,
          "seq": 0,
          "kind": "navigation",
          "message": "nav-to-home"
        },
        {
          "t": 2,
          "seq": 1,
          "kind": "console",
          "message": "hello world"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "console-middle-splice",
      "options": {
        "byteBudget": 16384,
        "consoleEntryCap": 20
      },
      "input": [
        {
          "t": 1,
          "seq": 0,
          "kind": "console",
          "message": "cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc"
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "t": 1,
          "seq": 0,
          "kind": "console",
          "message": "cccccccccc…[+10 chars]…cccccccccc",
          "truncated": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "bulky-evicted-before-structural",
      "options": {
        "byteBudget": 250,
        "consoleEntryCap": 100
      },
      "input": [
        {
          "t": 1,
          "seq": 0,
          "kind": "navigation",
          "message": "nav-to-home"
        },
        {
          "t": 2,
          "seq": 1,
          "kind": "console",
          "message": "cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc"
        },
        {
          "t": 3,
          "seq": 2,
          "kind": "console",
          "message": "dddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddd"
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "t": 1,
          "seq": 0,
          "kind": "navigation",
          "message": "nav-to-home"
        },
        {
          "t": 2,
          "seq": 1,
          "kind": "console",
          "level": "info",
          "message": "+1 console hidden",
          "data": {
            "droppedCount": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "t": 3,
          "seq": 2,
          "kind": "console",
          "message": "dddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddd"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
